\section{Interactive version}{

The workflow has a short-distance and an optional long-distance component:
\enumerate{
\item When loci contain multiple SNPs, choose the SNP-retention rule:
\code{1 = mac}, \code{2 = random}, \code{3 = first},
\code{4 = middle}, or \code{5 = last}.
\item Answer
\code{"Do you want to continue filtering using long distance ld? (y/n):"}.
Answering no returns after short-distance pruning.
\item For reference-guided data, choose whether missingness should determine
which SNP is retained from an LD group. De novo data currently uses basic
SNPRelate pruning.
\item Inspect the LD boxplot and answer
\code{"Enter the long LD threshold (filter.long.ld threshold, double/proportion):"}.
}
Use \code{interactive.filter = FALSE} and explicit short- and long-distance
settings for a reproducible analysis. The missingness-aware option is passed
as \code{long.ld.missing} through \code{...}.
}

